---
name: vibemon-sprite-reference
description: Generates a single canonical reference image for a Vibemon before posing.
version: 1.0.0
---
{%- set elements = vibemon.affinity.identity.elements -%}
{%- set role = vibemon.affinity.identity.battle_role[0] | lower -%}

Render ONE clean canonical reference image for a Pokémon-style creature named "{{ vibemon.affinity.identity.name }}".

PURPOSE
- This image will be used as the visual reference for a later nine-pose sprite sheet.
- Prioritize locked anatomy, readable silhouette, exact proportions, exact palette, and exact signature feature placement over dramatic posing.
- The creature must be easy to copy into many poses without redesigning it.

CANVAS RULES
- Background: flat matte {{ vibemon.aesthetic.background_color }} as ONE uniform wash filling every pixel that is not the creature.
- The background contains nothing else. No scenery, props, text, labels, UI, grid, shadows, glow, aura, floor line, weather marks, or decorative effects.
- Draw exactly one full-body creature in a neutral three-quarter view, turned just enough to show the back/dorsal silhouette and appendage roots clearly.
- Keep the whole creature inside frame with margin on all sides.

IDENTITY
- Name: {{ vibemon.affinity.identity.name }}
- Element(s): {{ elements | join(" / ") }}
{% if vibemon.affinity.identity.visual_notes %}
- Personality notes (do not infer anatomy from these): {{ vibemon.affinity.identity.visual_notes }}
{% endif %}

PRIMARY ELEMENT — {{ elements[0] | upper }} (canonical anatomy, palette, and motifs — the source of truth for what this creature looks like). The BODY ARCHETYPE below dictates the silhouette type. Role and tier modify posture, scale, and complexity but NEVER override the body archetype.
{% include "elements/" ~ elements[0] ~ ".j2" +%}

{% if elements | length > 1 %}
SECONDARY ELEMENT — {{ elements[1] | upper }} (accent layer only: extremities, markings, secondary materials — must never override the primary element's silhouette or palette)
{% include "elements/" ~ elements[1] ~ ".j2" +%}

{% endif %}
TIER
{% include "tiers/" ~ vibemon.affinity.identity.tier ~ "/visual.j2" +%}

ROLE
{% include "roles/" ~ vibemon.affinity.identity.battle_role.name | lower ~ ".j2" +%}
Role body-language cues describe attitude only. They must never add humanoid arms, hands, legs, shoulders, fists, palms, or upright posture if the chosen body archetype does not naturally have them.

INFLUENCES (translate into one simple anatomical feature, marking, material, or silhouette cue; do not add extra detached effects):
{% for affinity in vibemon.birth_affinities %}
{% if affinity.visual_notes %}
- {{ affinity.visual_notes }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

LOCKED DESIGN DECISIONS
- Choose one simple body plan from the primary element's BODY ARCHETYPE.
- Choose the exact appendage configuration once: number, type, root placement, size, and major shape for every arm, leg, flipper, wing, tail, fin, crest, shell, antenna, or tentacle.
- Choose at most the allowed number of signature features from the tier complexity budget.
- If a dorsal fin, shell, membrane, crest, mane, plate, tail, or other back feature exists, make its root, outline, size, and internal marking unmistakable. It must be attached anatomy, not a cape, prop, halo, or detached object.
- Do not include any alternate forms, extra pose variants, action marks, expressive symbols, or environmental storytelling.

PALETTE & STYLE
- Primary fill: {{ vibemon.aesthetic.primary_color }} — overrides the PRIMARY ELEMENT's color hex if they differ.
{% if elements | length > 1 %}
- Secondary fill (accent zones — extremities, markings, underbelly): {{ vibemon.aesthetic.secondary_color }}
{% endif %}
- Lineart: #3D2B1F Tobacco Brown. Never pure black or darker than #2A1E16.
- Highlights: #F5F5DC Cream. Never pure white.
- Highlights must stay inside the creature silhouette only.
- Shadows: warm-shifted darker variants of the fill, mixed toward Tobacco Brown. Never black or cool gray.
- Aesthetic: Pokémon Sugimori — flat cel shading, clean confident lineart, warm gradient fills, Kodachrome-warmed and desaturated.

FINAL CHECK BEFORE DRAWING
- The image must look like the definitive model of one creature, not a scene and not a pose sheet.
- Every future pose should be able to copy this exact silhouette, proportions, palette, appendage count, and signature feature placement.
